member.remarks:
Game_EnableMusic and Game_DisableMusic. Turning it off stops whatever is playing;
turning it back on restarts the state's track from its beginning, which is what the original does
— it has nowhere to remember a position.

remarks.para:
This is the layer that makes a name mean anything. SoundBank holds AI_DEATH_01;
game code asks for ai_death_1; only the definition joins them, and it carries the distances
and the loop flag with it.

example.code:
public sealed partial class Igi2SwitchTask : Igi2Task
{
    [LevelService] public Func<string, MefModel?>? Models { get; set; }
    [LevelService] public Igi2Sounds? Sounds { get; set; }
}

// Task_DeclareParameters("HeightMap", "Position","ObjectPos", "Level","Int32", "Size","Int32", ...)
public sealed partial class HeightMap : GameTask
{
    [ScriptParam(ScriptParamType.ObjectPos, "Position")] public Vector3d Position;
    [ScriptParam(ScriptParamType.Int32, "Level")] public int Level;
    [ScriptParam(ScriptParamType.Int32, "Size")] public int Size;
}

member.param:
One exit function per state, run by  on the state being left, or
 for none. I.G.I. 2's machine carries this table (State_s.apfExitState);
I.G.I. 1's does not.
